B.aHd=new A.S(B.aLd,["Interest exploration test","What do you enjoy?","Let us start with the activities that catch your attention.","How do you think?","How you approach problems and information.","How do you like to work?","Your environment and your preferred way of getting things done.","People and communication","Collaborating, helping, and explaining ideas.","Science and technology","Your scientific and technical curiosity.","Creativity and expression","How you make new ideas and experiences.","Leadership and business","Initiative, persuasion, and building opportunities.","Your working style","What environment helps you keep going?","A more precise result","Optional extra questions that test how consistent your interests are.","Given completely free time to learn a brand-new skill, what would you most likely choose?","Take a device or tool apart to understand how it works inside and fix it.","Find a topic that interests me and read about it from several sources until I understand it deeply.","Try a new way to express myself (drawing, photography, writing) and make something of my own.","A friend asked for your help with a problem of theirs \u2014 what is closest to your reaction?","Sit with them, listen closely, and help them understand the problem themselves.","Suggest a practical plan right away and get them started on it today.","Ask for precise details first so I can lay out the solution step by step.","What draws you most when you meet a new system or app?","Trying to understand how it works inside and thinking about how it could be built or improved.","Analysing the numbers and data it produces to find a useful pattern.","Arranging how I use it into clear, fixed steps I never deviate from.","You face a complex problem in a school or personal project \u2014 what do you do first?","Break it into small parts and solve each one with clear logic.","Look for similar solutions others have tried and compare them using evidence and numbers.","Try the first idea that comes to mind and adjust it if it does not work.","Important information is missing a piece, and you need to decide right now \u2014 what do you do?","Decide quickly with the best estimate available, then adjust later if needed.","Ask for a short delay to gather as much of the missing detail as possible before deciding.","Consult someone whose judgement I trust before I decide.","You get results or data with a small contradiction in them \u2014 how do you usually handle it?","Notice it quickly and check every number to find the source of the error.","Think of more than one possible explanation before deciding which is right.","I usually do not notice it unless someone points it out to me.","At the end of a good work day, what makes you feel most satisfied?","Seeing a tangible result I made with my own hands or in front of my eyes.","Completing a step within a long plan that I know is leading to a bigger goal.","Talking with people and leaving a clear mark on their day.","Which work environment suits you best?","Clear standards and steps, so I know exactly what is expected of me.","A free space where I manage my own time and tasks without constant supervision.","A daily-changing environment where I do not know exactly what will happen.","A long project stretches on for weeks with no quick payoff \u2014 what is your honest reaction?","I keep going with focus, because the final idea is worth the patience.","I keep going, but I need to split it into small weekly tasks to feel progress.","I usually lose enthusiasm, and I prefer tasks whose results show within days.","Which kind of daily task do you usually prefer?","Working with a team I discuss things with constantly and draw energy from.","Working alone with simple, rare coordination with others.","Leading a small group and dividing the roles between us.","Someone explains an idea, and some people around do not understand it \u2014 what do you do?","Explain it again in a different way that suits each person.","Leave it to the person with the idea \u2014 explaining is not my role.","Ask questions to find out exactly where it went wrong.","A friend shares a personal problem that is bothering them \u2014 what is your closest reaction?","Listen first without interrupting until they finish, then help them think through a solution.","Give them the direct solution quickly to save their time.","I feel uncomfortable with this kind of conversation and try to move past it gently.","You notice a strange phenomenon (why the sky changes colour, why a plant grows a certain way...) \u2014 what is your reaction?","Look for the scientific explanation and verify it with an experiment or evidence if possible.","I am mildly interested but forget about it quickly.","Ask someone I trust to know instead of researching it myself.","You need to learn a completely new tool or program for something \u2014 what is your closest feeling?","Excited \u2014 I love discovering new tools even if they are complex.","I learn it because I have to, but I do not enjoy the process.","I would rather someone else handle the technical part while I follow the rest.","Which is closest to how you think when dealing with numbers or equations?","I enjoy finding a pattern or a solution to a complex numerical problem.","I deal with them when I have to, but it is not something I enjoy.","I avoid them as much as possible and look for another way to solve the problem that does not need numbers.","You are designing a presentation or a post \u2014 what occupies you most?","Visual balance, colour, and how elements are arranged.","The words used and how clear the written message is.","Getting it done as quickly as possible without focusing much on how it looks.","Important instructions for a new task are missing or unclear \u2014 what do you do?","Invent a sensible starting point myself and continue, adjusting if I get it wrong.","Ask for full clarification before taking a single step.","Look for a similar ready-made model and copy it instead of inventing my own.","You have a first idea for a creative project (a story, a design, a video) \u2014 what is your next step?","Improve it again and again, trying different versions until I am convinced by the result.","Execute it exactly as it came to me, without much revision.","Share the initial idea with others to hear their opinion before I finish it.","A group needs someone to take the first step and nobody is doing it \u2014 what do you usually do?","I take the initiative myself to organise the first step and divide the tasks.","I wait a little; if nobody starts, I contribute an idea rather than full leadership.","I would rather join someone else's plan than start one myself.","You notice a recurring problem people around you suffer from (lost time, a missing service...) \u2014 what is your reaction?","Think about turning it into a project or service idea that actually solves the problem.","Complain about it with others but do not think about solving it myself.","Analyse the technical cause of the problem more than I think about a business opportunity in it.","You need to make a decision that could go wrong, on behalf of your whole team \u2014 how do you act?","Take the decision with confidence after understanding the worst case, and own the outcome.","I would rather delay the decision until more than one person shares it with me.","I feel a lot of pressure from the idea of carrying a decision like this.","Which work pattern can you imagine being comfortable with in the long run?","Flexible work that lets me do a large part of it from anywhere.","A fixed workplace where I connect face to face with my team every day.","The place matters less to me than having varied tasks from one day to the next.","Several important tasks pile up in a tight time frame \u2014 how do you usually act?","Stay calm and organise my priorities step by step.","I feel clear pressure but get it done anyway.","I get stressed in a way that affects my focus until the hard period ends.","Years after graduating, which description is closest to what you hope for yourself professionally?","Still learning new things continuously in my field.","Mastered a specific field and practise it steadily without big changes.","Changed direction or added a skill completely different from what I started with.","A tool or device breaks during an important project \u2014 what do you actually do?","Try to diagnose the cause myself first before asking for help or a replacement.","Ask someone more experienced for immediate help to save time.","Replace it or work around it with a backup plan without trying to fix it.","You read two completely opposing views on the same subject \u2014 what do you do?","Carefully compare each side's evidence before forming my own opinion.","I lean towards whichever view seems logical at first glance, without much depth.","I would rather not get involved in topics that are disputed at all.","A large table of numbers or data sits in front of you with no clear explanation \u2014 what do you do?","Try to discover a pattern in it myself, even if it takes time.","Ask a specialist to summarise what the table means.","Ignore it unless it is truly essential to my work.","Work needs coordinating between several people who disagree \u2014 which role do you prefer?","Mediate between them and coordinate until they reach agreement.","Do my own part precisely and leave the coordination to someone else.","Withdraw from this kind of task if I can.","You are with someone going through a difficult human situation who needs real support \u2014 how do you act?","Stay calm and offer steady support without it affecting me too heavily.","I get so affected along with them that it becomes hard for me to think clearly.","I would rather someone closer to them handle this kind of situation.","A creative idea has not yet reached the perfect shape in your mind \u2014 what do you do?","Keep improving it gradually instead of waiting for a perfect moment of inspiration.","Stop until a clearly better idea comes to me.","Execute it as it is now \u2014 perfection is not needed for every piece.","Before suggesting an idea or product to someone, what step matters most to you?","Making sure I truly understand what they need before suggesting anything.","Presenting my best right away and letting them judge it.","I hesitate a lot about taking the initiative to suggest something to someone else.","Work needs careful review because a mistake would be costly \u2014 how do you handle it?","Review it against a clear checklist, step by step, before handing it in.","Give it one quick pass \u2014 I generally trust my own work.","I would rather someone more meticulous than me review it."],t.w)
